oracle: host CPython 3.11.17, 3.12.3, 3.13.16 (python3.11, python3.12, python3.13)
command: {python3.11,python3.12,python3.13} -I literals.py
result: exit 0; stdout is exactly <name>.expect
releases: 3.11.17, 3.12.3 and 3.13.16 by their own host interpreters (above); 3.5.10, 3.6.0 and 3.16.0a1 through the py3 profile's pinned-source evidence (python-iir-compiler/src/profiles.rs)
why: every literal form (`D.D`, `.D`, `D.`, leading zeros, exponents) is correctly rounded and printed as repr: shortest round trip, fixed notation for exponents -4..15, else `d.ddde±XX`; no arithmetic, so the IIR is only consts and write_f64_py
